problems.problem:
Let $m$ and $n$ be two positive integers and let $A_1, \dots, A_m$ be sets of positive integers such that:

(1) $A_i$ and $A_j$ are disjoint for all distinct indices $i$ and $j$;

(2) $|A_i| = n$, $i = 1, \dots, m$;

(3) For every index $i$, no element of $A_i$ is divisible by any element of $A_{i+1}$, where indices are taken modulo $m$.

Determine the maximum number of ordered pairs $(a, b)$, where $a$ and $b$ are elements of different $A_i$'s and $b$ is divisible by $a$.

For each positive integer $n > 1$, denote by $p(n)$ the largest prime factor of $n$. Determine all triples $x, y, z$ of distinct positive integers which simultaneously satisfy the conditions:

(1) $x, y, z$ are in arithmetic progression;

(2) $p(xyz) \le 3$.
